Build succeeds. Here's a summary of all breaking changes identified and the fixes applied:

---

## Breaking Changes Fixed in This Project

| # | Breaking Change | Fix |
|---|----------------|-----|
| 1 | TFM `net8.0` → `net9.0`, packages 8.0→9.0 | Updated `.csproj` |
| 2 | `DateTime.UtcNow` in `HasData` causes "pending model changes" exception | Replaced with fixed constant `new DateTime(2024,1,1,0,0,0,DateTimeKind.Utc)` |
| 3 | `Migrate()` inside explicit transaction now throws | Removed wrapping transaction/strategy — EF Core 9 manages its own |
| 4 | `Design` package fails with SDK 9.0.200+ | Added `<IncludeAssets>` and `<Publish>true</Publish>` |

---

## Cosmos DB Project Breaking Changes (separate project)

For your Cosmos DB provider project, apply these fixes in `OnModelCreating`:

```csharp
// 1. Discriminator property renamed from "Discriminator" to "$type".
//    Preserve old name for existing documents:
modelBuilder.Entity<YourEntity>().HasDiscriminator<string>("Discriminator");

// 2. id property no longer embeds discriminator (was "Type|Key", now just "Key").
//    Preserve old format for existing documents:
modelBuilder.Entity<YourEntity>().HasRootDiscriminatorInJsonId(true);

// 3. Sync I/O now throws. Replace all synchronous calls:
//    .ToList()       → await .ToListAsync()
//    .First()        → await .FirstAsync()
//    .SaveChanges()  → await .SaveChangesAsync()
```
